    {
        "content": "<p>Theodus edited <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14607\">PR #14607</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Restricts the <code>amode_imm_reg_iadd</code> lowering rule for i32 to avoid introducing unnecessary register pressure.</p>\n<p>Before these changes, this rule would result in the following transformation (the added <code>%shared_i32</code> test):</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">v2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iadd</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"kt\">i32</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v1</span>\n<span class=\"n\">v3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iconst</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"kt\">i32</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">100</span>\n<span class=\"n\">v4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iadd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v2</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v3</span>\n<span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v2</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v4</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>lowered to</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">leal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">rdi</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">rsi</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">eax</span>\n<span class=\"n\">leal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mh\">0x64</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">rdi</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">rsi</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">edx</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>which extends the live ranges of <code>v0</code> and <code>v1</code> despite their sum being available via the returned value <code>v2</code>.</p>\n<p>The updated rule reuses the shared i32 sum as the base register:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">leal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">rdi</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">rsi</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">eax</span>\n<span class=\"n\">leal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mh\">0x64</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">rax</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">edx</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Folding remains unrestricted for i64 sums, allowing loads/stores to use base+index directly.</p>\n<h2>additional context</h2>\n<p>This behavior was discovered through performance analysis of a ChaCha20 implementation where this added register pressure made a significant difference in throughput (measured on AMD Ryzen AI Max+ 395):</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">ChaCha double-round instructions</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">stack operations</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\">throughput gain</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">163 → 141</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">52 → 37</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+7.3%</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 629934186,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1791397585
